From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:17:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 311/311] fate/source: list the local V4L2 stateless uAPI
 headers

The VC-1, MPEG-4 Part 2/H.263, AVS and AVS2 V4L2 Request hwaccels carry
copies of their kernel uAPI definitions (libavcodec/v4l2-stateless-*.h),
used until linux/v4l2-controls.h and linux/videodev2.h provide them. They
keep the kernel uAPI SPDX licence line rather than an FFmpeg licence
header, so add them to the list of files without a standard header.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 tests/ref/fate/source | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/ref/fate/source b/tests/ref/fate/source
index 78d3a2e0fa..3129afda09 100644
--- a/tests/ref/fate/source
+++ b/tests/ref/fate/source
@@ -4,6 +4,10 @@ libavcodec/interplayacm.c
 libavcodec/log2_tab.c
 libavcodec/reverse.c
 libavcodec/riscv/cpu_common.c
+libavcodec/v4l2-stateless-avs.h
+libavcodec/v4l2-stateless-avs2.h
+libavcodec/v4l2-stateless-mpeg4.h
+libavcodec/v4l2-stateless-vc1.h
 libavdevice/file_open.c
 libavdevice/reverse.c
 libavdevice/riscv/cpu_common.c
